  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1018 PM CDT Thu Jul 16 2026\n\nExpect additional rain and storm chances on Sunday as a surface\nboundary drops southward into or completely through Middle\nTennessee. Temperatures will continue to exceed seasonal norms by\na degree or two, with heat indices topping out in the low 100s\nthrough the weekend and into early next week. However, the\natmosphere will finally dry out considerably following Sunday's\nfropa (fingers crossed!), so rain and storm chances next week will\nbe a great deal lower. Temperatures will peak on Tuesday, with\nmany spots reaching the mid 90s. There's also the possibility that\nenough locations will experience heat indices of 105+ that a Heat\nAdvisory would be needed, but that's still a several days away. A\nsecond fropa on Wednesday would bring temperatures back down to \nseasonal norms and also keep heat indices below 100 degrees for \nthe remainder of next week.",
